# Skill: feature-developer

Read and follow `skills/feature-developer/SKILL.md`. Use templates in `skills/feature-developer/templates/` and fields in `skills/feature-developer/schema.json`.

Announce: `Using skill: feature-developer`.

## Phases (mandatory order)

1. Capability Discovery -- tests, CI, linters, docs layout; evidence paths only.
2. Spec and architecture blueprint -- `docs/features/<kebab-name>/`.
3. Human review gate -- STOP. No code until `APPROVED: feature-developer Phase 3`.
4. TDD implementation -- failing test, minimum code, refactor; do not expand scope.
5. Security and edge-case audit -- STRIDE on touched boundaries; high/critical accept-risk needs a human owner.
6. Docs freeze and global sync -- spec/architecture become immutable.
7. CI verification if present, else structured manual QA with evidence.

## Adaptive flags

- `tests.automated`: runner and command evidenced. Still write tests if false.
- `ci.present`: CI config evidenced. Do not claim CI passed if absent.
- `lint.blocking`: lint in CI or documented hook. Clean touched files before freeze.

## Do not use

When the request is still ambiguous (use `feature-specifier`), when the user only wants an ADR or threat model, or for trivial non-behavioral edits.

On `REJECTED: feature-developer Phase 3`, revise planning artifacts and resubmit the gate. Do not code.
